{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting.\n    Sorting order depends on the parity of the sum of the first and last elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    first_element = array[0]\n    last_element = array[-1]\n    sum_first_last = first_element + last_element\n\n    # If sum is odd, sort ascending (reverse=False). If even, sort descending (reverse=True).\n    sort_descending = (sum_first_last % 2 == 0)\n\n    return sorted(array, reverse=sort_descending)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds occurrences of x in a 2D ragged list and returns their (row, column)\n    coordinates, sorted by row ascending, then column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    class Coordinate:\n        \"\"\"Represents a zero-indexed (row, column) coordinate with custom comparison.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, row: int, col: int):\n            self.row = row\n            self.col = col\n\n        def __lt__(self, other: object) -> bool:\n            if self.row != other.row:\n                return self.row < other.row\n            return self.col > other.col # Sort column descending\n\n    found_coords = []\n    for r_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for c_idx, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val == x:\n                found_coords.append(Coordinate(r_idx, c_idx))\n\n    sorted_coords = sorted(found_coords)\n    return [(c.row, c.col) for c in sorted_coords]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/90", "solution": "```python\ndef next_smallest(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given a list of integers.\n    Write a function next_smallest() that returns the 2nd smallest element of the list.\n    Return None if there is no such element.\n\n    next_smallest([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]) == 2\n    next_smallest([5, 1, 4, 3, 2]) == 2\n    next_smallest([]) == None\n    next_smallest([1, 1]) == None\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_sorted_elements = sorted(list(set(lst)))\n\n    if len(unique_sorted_elements) < 2:\n        return None\n    else:\n        return unique_sorted_elements[1]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Create a function encrypt that takes a string as an argument and\n    returns a string encrypted with the alphabet being rotated.\n    The alphabet should be rotated in a manner such that the letters\n    shift down by two multiplied to two places.\n    For example:\n    encrypt('hi') returns 'lm'\n    encrypt('asdfghjkl') returns 'ewhjklnop'\n    encrypt('gf') returns 'kj'\n    encrypt('et') returns 'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    # The shift amount is two multiplied by two, which equals 4.\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n\n    def _shift_char(char: str, shift: int) -> str:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            start = ord('a')\n            return chr(start + (ord(char) - start + shift) % 26)\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            start = ord('A')\n            return chr(start + (ord(char) - start + shift) % 26)\n        return char\n\n    encrypted_chars = [_shift_char(char, SHIFT_AMOUNT) for char in s]\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)"}
