{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function that takes a string and returns an ordered version of it.\n    Ordered version of string, is a string where all words (separated by space)\n    are replaced by a new word where all the characters arranged in\n    ascending order based on ascii value.\n    \"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    current_word_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char == ' ':\n            # If we've accumulated characters for a word, sort them and add to parts\n            if current_word_chars:\n                parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(current_word_chars)))\n                current_word_chars = []\n            # Add the space\n            parts.append(' ')\n        else:\n            # Accumulate characters for the current word\n            current_word_chars.append(char)\n\n    # After the loop, if there are any remaining characters, they form the last word\n    if current_word_chars:\n        parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(current_word_chars)))\n\n    return \"\".join(parts)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement a function that takes a non-negative integer and returns an array of the first n\n    integers that are prime numbers and less than n.\n    for example:\n    count_up_to(5) => [2,3]\n    count_up_to(11) => [2,3,5,7]\n    count_up_to(0) => []\n    count_up_to(20) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19]\n    count_up_to(1) => []\n    count_up_to(18) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17]\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num):\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        # Check for factors from 2 up to the square root of num.\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    primes = []\n    # Iterate from 2 up to n-1 to find prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            primes.append(i)\n    return primes"}
